{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.99,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"DP counts binary strings of length 14 avoiding 000 and 111.\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 identical bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of valid strings length n. We can use DP with states: last run length and last bit. Equivalent to sequences avoiding 3 same in a row. Let dp[n][k][b] where k=1 or 2 length of current run, b=0/1. Transition: if k=1, can add same bit to get k=2; or add opposite bit to start new run length1. If k=2, cannot add same bit (would make 3), so must add opposite bit to start new run length1. Base n=1: dp[1][1][0]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. Compute up to n=14. Let's compute quickly.\n\nWe'll compute totals.\n\nLet A_n = number of strings length n ending with run length1 (i.e., last two bits different or n=1). Let B_n = number ending with run length2 (last two bits same, but previous different). Then recurrence:\n\nFrom A_{n-1}: can add same bit -> becomes B_n. can add opposite -> becomes A_n.\n\nFrom B_{n-1}: can only add opposite -> becomes A_n.\n\nThus:\n\nA_n = A_{n-1} (opposite) + B_{n-1} (opposite) = A_{n-1} + B_{n-1}\nB_n = A_{n-1} (same) + 0 = A_{n-1}\n\nBase n=1: A_1=2 (both bits), B_1=0.\n\nCompute:\n\nn=2:\nA_2 = A1 + B1 =2+0=2\nB_2 = A1 =2\n\nn=3:\nA3 = A2 + B2 =2+2=4\nB3 = A2 =2\n\nn=4:\nA4 = A3 + B3 =4+2=6\nB4 = A3 =4\n\nn=5:\nA5 = A4 + B4 =6+4=10\nB5 = A4 =6\n\nn=6:\nA6 =10+6=16\nB6 =10\n\nn=7:\nA7 =16+10=26\nB7 =16\n\nn=8:\nA8 =26+16=42\nB8 =26\n\nn=9:\nA9 =42+26=68\nB9 =42\n\nn=10:\nA10=68+42=110\nB10=68\n\nn=11:\nA11=110+68=178\nB11=110\n\nn=12:\nA12=178+110=288\nB12=178\n\nn=13:\nA13=288+178=466\nB13=288\n\nn=14:\nA14=466+288=754\nB14=466\n\nTotal strings length14 = A14 + B14 = 754 + 466 = 1220.\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON with decision answer."}}],"created":1790954447,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":743,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4854,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-8iwDuGYaeIUnP237F3Dw8gxUXPl9l9Mb","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":485.855,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.11818414011189492,"prompt_per_second":8461.372220106821,"predicted_n":743,"predicted_ms":2239.056,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0175956873315366,"predicted_per_second":331.3896570697651}}